{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20294",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.28,
      "end_seconds": 10.13,
      "duration_seconds": 8.85,
      "text": "Doctor, the patient's with us now. I did the usual checks at the front, so just say when you want them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 12.21,
      "end_seconds": 16.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Great. Hello, come in and sit down. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.22,
      "end_seconds": 24.31,
      "duration_seconds": 7.09,
      "text": "Yeah, um, it's a cut on my finger. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 26.19,
      "end_seconds": 37.2,
      "duration_seconds": 11.01,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Oxygen saturation is 98 percent, pulse 73, respiratory rate 14. Temperature is 36.5 degrees, pressure 109 over 81."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.5,
      "end_seconds": 39.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.94,
      "end_seconds": 58.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.17,
      "end_seconds": 61.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "It's been two days now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.03,
      "end_seconds": 71.79,
      "duration_seconds": 8.76,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.61,
      "end_seconds": 76.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "A dressing helps a bit. It's worse with gripping."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 77.71,
      "end_seconds": 80.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Has there been a numb fingertip too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.26,
      "end_seconds": 89.35,
      "duration_seconds": 7.09,
      "text": "Yes, for two weeks. Right, about numb fingertip, it happens every other day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.43,
      "end_seconds": 96.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "Have you had a cut on your finger before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.61,
      "end_seconds": 106.09,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "A bit, a couple of years ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.23,
      "end_seconds": 118.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Alright, have you had any dirt in the wound or pus?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.45,
      "end_seconds": 122.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.95,
      "end_seconds": 125.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "And what about fever or bite?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.48,
      "end_seconds": 128.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "No, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.56,
      "end_seconds": 132.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.39,
      "end_seconds": 137.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "That's normal as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.81,
      "end_seconds": 141.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.58,
      "end_seconds": 145.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.72,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.1,
      "end_seconds": 150.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Okay, any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.75,
      "end_seconds": 152.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Yes, asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.06,
      "end_seconds": 156.76,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.92,
      "end_seconds": 174.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.93,
      "end_seconds": 186.76,
      "duration_seconds": 10.83,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. I'm vegetarian and have been for years. I live with my elderly mother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.42,
      "end_seconds": 192.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.41,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.38,
      "end_seconds": 196.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.65,
      "end_seconds": 201.65,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.04,
      "end_seconds": 205.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "It's Asthalin inhaler, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.73,
      "end_seconds": 209.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.88,
      "end_seconds": 215.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "I mean, you know, no, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.48,
      "end_seconds": 220.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.84,
      "end_seconds": 221.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.45,
      "end_seconds": 224.76,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.47,
      "end_seconds": 245.9,
      "duration_seconds": 9.43,
      "text": "There is a two-centimetre clean cut over the first knuckle, the finger moves fully and the fingertip feels normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.08,
      "end_seconds": 272.06,
      "duration_seconds": 23.98,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. Taking everything into account, this looks most like a clean finger laceration without nerve or tendon injury. A tendon injury is still possible. I'd like to arrange an X-ray of the finger for laceration. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 273.39,
      "end_seconds": 277.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Ah, where would I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.86,
      "end_seconds": 301.41,
      "duration_seconds": 22.55,
      "text": "I'd like you to take tetanus booster, 0.5 ml, once, for one day. That's for tetanus prevention. Keep the dressing dry for two days and watch for redness or pus. If the wound becomes red, hot or swollen, that's the point to come in urgently. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.42,
      "end_seconds": 306.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.95,
      "end_seconds": 308.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}